{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854508-migrating-to-the-beast-courts","id":854508,"title":"Migrating to the beast courts.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-28T09:09:36-07:00","id":854508,"title":"Migrating to the beast courts.","content":"Short story- I'm playing a character who likes travel and agressively tries to learn things so that nothing will ever catch her with her pants down. Her whole thing as a ragabash has been to scrutinise weaknesses and strengthen allies, especially herself, for the apocalypse, so she wants to look to the east and africa to see how things are done in different systems, because garou are so often fools. Also learning the secrets of other changers is a sure way to get strong.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now the ahadi is great <i>(and not because I'm playing a Black get with that questionable Uktena ancestry)</i> Because you simply prove your worth, get inducted with a ceremony, and carry on as normal with a bit more cooperation with other breeds.<i> It doesn't yet exist in the timeline we're in. I could help out in the war against blacktooth though. </i><br /> <br /> <br /> Now In the beast courts, joining looks like a mess, and they haven't really explained the options that well. <i>A 4th rank Khan owes her a favour and the stargazer teaching her Kailendo in a bone gnawer sept buggered off because she might have helped a Khan kill a close friend of his, so she has reasons to go east. </i><br /> <br /> But, well, from what I read, the possibilities of joining the beast courts are limiting/confusing<br /> -Cast of my old renown system (Honour for virtue, do I keep wisdom and glory where they are?),maybe start from rank 1, and get a new auspice and join a mountain sentai. Wear a nice badge.<br /> An additional note- Virtue Is the same thing as honour. This isn't good for other changers, but can't garou just cheat and pay lip service to both?<br /> -Keep my normal renown, Join a wave sentai with or without an auspice.... I'm not sure if you can get a beast court auspice with this method. Not sure if you get to wear a badge with this method either.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now resetting rank is pretty unacceptable to this character. Offending an entire brood of spirits so seriously just isn't something considerable (especially when you've got the renown to be fourth rank. Still third, but that's because my character's too young for it to be wise to advance. ) (also she's a pretty serious collector of gifts) Now, Judging by Khan and hakken, she doesn't actually have to leave tribe (technically) or auspice,so maybe the eternal enmity of the spirits isn't going to be a problem, but the rank reset is (even though the character's younger than she should be for her rank, but she would likely plan to re-enter the garou nation after a few years). I suspect that the western stargazers didn't all loose their rank when they left the garou nation for the courts, that would've been a terrible decision to turn Athro and elder into 'wood', but it wouldn't be a great decision to deny an elder stargazer duties in courts (should they ever get their heads out of the clouds and ask)<br /> <br /> \u200bAny solutions? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T16:09:58-07:00","id":854713,"title":"","content":"When you join an organization, you typically start from the bottom, so you get to be a Rank 1 member of a given Beast Courts auspice, just like a renunciate. This involves undergoing a similar rite. Rejoining the Garou Nation, if they let you, would follow the same procedure.<br /> <br /> Virtue is similar to the Garou conception of Honor. However, it's a bit more inclusive, since you need to be of a mind to think of Fera as comrades and not simply threats.<br /> <br /> It's uncertain where elder Stargazers sat after the sides switched, but it's entirely possible that they might have been given trials to prove their worth as a kind of formality. Then again, the Beast Courts were always more accepting of them than outsiders of other tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T00:35:09-07:00","id":858814,"title":"","content":"Greetings...<br /> <br /> I have some ideas, please find them below in black.I must mention, that it's my interpretation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854508-migrating-to-the-beast-courts#post854508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Short story- I'm playing a character who likes travel and agressively <b>(In the Courts you should be polite &amp; courtly, not agressive. That's the surest way to get back home.)</b> tries to learn things so that nothing will ever catch her with her pants down. <b>(The First Ronin will ALWAYS get you pants down.)</b> Her whole thing as a ragabash has been to scrutinise weaknesses and strengthen allies, especially herself, for the apocalypse, so she wants to look to the east and africa to see how things are done in different systems, because garou are so often fools. Also learning the secrets of other changers is a sure way to get strong.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now the ahadi is great <i>(and not because I'm playing a Black get with that questionable Uktena ancestry)</i> Because you simply prove your worth, get inducted with a ceremony, and carry on as normal with a bit more cooperation with other breeds.<i> It doesn't yet exist in the timeline we're in. I could help out in the war against blacktooth though. </i><br /> <br /> <br /> Now In the beast courts, joining looks like a mess, and they haven't really explained the options that well. <b>(It's stated clearly - I hade to chack it myself, becouse one of my character: There is a Rite in the Hengeyokai book, which is similar in all of the effect to the Rite of Renucitation, you will be stripped from your Rank, Renown &amp; start as a 1st Rank sth., but you can regain your Gifts.)</b> <i>A 4th rank Khan owes her a favour and the stargazer teaching her Kailendo in a bone gnawer sept buggered off because she might have helped a Khan kill a close friend of his, so she has reasons to go east. </i><br /> <br /> But, well, from what I read, the possibilities of joining the beast courts are limiting/confusing<br /> -Cast of my old renown system (Honour for virtue, do I keep wisdom and glory where they are?),maybe start from rank 1, and get a new auspice and join a mountain sentai. Wear a nice badge.<br /> An additional note- Virtue Is the same thing as honour. This isn't good for other changers, but can't garou just cheat and pay lip service to both? <b>(No, you may be able (if you're very pro in lieing to thousands year old mind-reading dragons) to cheat the Shen, but you won't be able to do this with the Spirits which enpower the Rites, Gifts, etc. By the way, beeing a two faced liar is the best way to loose all of your Honor &amp; much of your Wisdom. The Hengeyokai book also states, that there is no known Sunset People, who succesfuly get introduced to the Court -not counting the Stargasers. Garous are always treated with great care, but if you will be able to get a Bunyip, who votes for your acceptance, it's a different matter.)</b><br /> -Keep my normal renown, Join a wave sentai with or without an auspice.... I'm not sure if you can get a beast court auspice with this method. Not sure if you get to wear a badge with this method either. <b>(You may be accepted as a temproal ally, but you won't become a member. Your greatest chances is with solitary Court Members, who travel abroad, for example Kitsunes, who travel far.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Now resetting rank is pretty unacceptable to this character. <b>(You have to sacrifice something for your advancement. Odin, the All-Father hung 9 days hanged &amp; pierced throught with his spear to get the runes. Worse than some Renown.)</b> Offending <b>(You don't offend them, you gain their ACCPETANCE throught SACRIFICE.)</b> an entire brood of spirits so seriously just isn't something considerable (especially when you've got the renown to be fourth rank. Still third, but that's because my character's too young for it to be wise to advance. <b>(That's a sad excuse from a ST?)</b>) (also she's a pretty serious collector of gifts<b>(You won't loose them.</b>) Now, Judging by Khan and hakken, she doesn't actually have to leave tribe (technically) <b>(No, you would be still a Get, still a Ragabash, but you would receive new, additional Mandates, tasks, etc.)</b> or auspice,so maybe the eternal enmity of the spirits isn't going to be a problem, but the rank reset is (even though the character's younger than she should be for her rank, but she would likely plan to re-enter the garou nation <b>(You won't be able to re-enter the Nation, the Rite of Reunciation just works as a one way ticket) </b>after a few years). I suspect that the western stargazers didn't all loose their rank when they left the garou nation for the courts, that would've been a terrible decision to turn Athro and elder into 'wood', but it wouldn't be a great decision to deny an elder stargazer duties in courts (should they ever get their heads out of the clouds and ask) <b>(They were a whole Tribe, not just one ini-tiny wolfi &amp; they didn't left the Courts. Theye were working for the Courts with an reversed integration project.</b><br /> <br /> \u200bAny solutions?</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope I helped. I'm open for further discussions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T04:24:54-07:00","id":858878,"title":"","content":"Firstly, Odin is hated by the Get of Fenrir, he's a monster of the wyrm, probably a leech. A terrible example to use. <br /> <br /> The character has a real fear/hatred of weakness. She heals the few scars she gets, trains constantly, spends her free time on spirit quests to gain more power. When she's not making herself stronger, she tries to teach others to get stronger. Resetting rank... A few steps back does not make a step forward. <br /> <br /> So... wave sentai might be fun? <br /> <br /> Massively offtopic bit about rank and age<br /> It makes sense that my character is held back because of my age (Nah, it's the ST doing time poorly) She's been a garou for only four years but I've hit 7 glory, 5 honour and 6 wisdom (and the storyteller is really stingy with honour, due to some bias against ragabash that he's taken a little too strongly. Also I'm close to having 8 glory and 7 wisdom). An early first change for a lupus character has meant I'm only five years old and looks about 15 (with two litters). That said, I've certainly got the XP expenditure to be considered the appropriate rank and 'more gifts than god' (We rollplay for gifts rather than buy them with xp, because In a tiny game we both think that's better. But he's not always good with giving out appropriate gifts, so I've got Grandmother's touch, Pure Identity and the kitsune gift 'seduction'... <br /> Maybe I'm the problem because my storyteller often wants to do big timeskips and Implies I've done nothing in them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T04:56:04-07:00","id":858895,"title":"","content":"About Odin: I threw him as a &quot;real&quot; mythologic figure without regard of the WoD status. In WoD there was a leech which took (a 4th gen. gangrel Matuselah) / ushurped it's name, identity &amp; place.<br /> From it's perspective the example is really terrible.<br /> <br /> About the character's relation to weakness: If you feel so strongly about weaknes,you will be obsessed by hunting for power &amp; it's a new form of personal flaw, so frankly, a weakness. It's the path into the Wyrm's Maw (ask the infernalists, BSDs, some Abominations). - Let's swim in he silver of Erebus. It helps negating the unhealthy ideas a bit.<br /> <br /> About Lupuses's First Change: It usually occurs at age of 2, at maturation, so it was a LATE one.<br /> <br /> About age: No, it doesn't make sense. Evan Heals-the-Past is a whelp (by age), but a respected leader &amp; great Philodox. Karin Jarlsd\u00f6ttir was 25 when she become a Jarl (by Caern status) &amp; Athro by Rank. I think your ST just don't want to give you juicy level 4 Gifts.<br /> <br /> About learning Gifts: It sould be handed for BOTH roleplaying &amp; Xp. If they would be free you could receive almost 20 Gift / day (if you sit in an appropiate Caern &amp; have a Theurge with sufficiently hight Gnosis to summon actively helpful spirits &amp; you have a Kinfolk who brings you hamburger.)<br /> <br /> The last one is a flaw of the ST. Why don't you talk him / her about it?<br /> <br /> <b>By the way: How the hack became a Get Lupus a black woman?</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":562,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","user":"Lachdanan","date":". 04-04-2016, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T05:54:03-07:00","id":858926,"title":"","content":"There's Odin the God, There's Wotan the Vampire warlord of the Dark Ages... they are not the same. Fenris however, is the bane of Odin (who was most likely a mage cum god cum wyrmspawn), and sadly, vice versa...<br /> <br /> If the Wolf's human ge makes him a teenage boy, he has barely been active a couple of years. One could easily argue that's too short for Rank 4.<br /> <br /> ... and Karin Jarlsd\u00f6ttir is FEMALE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 04-04-2016, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T06:07:07-07:00","id":858934,"title":"","content":"Asmodai!<br /> <br /> Yeh, I know the difference (by the way, Odin &amp; Wotan are tha names of a semi-equivalent deity based on different region/religion). In WoD Odin &amp; Wotan are both mentioned as a hell of an old Gangrel &amp; they may be the same old bloodsucker.<br /> <br /> About Karin: Sorry, English is only my second language &amp; I mainly speak a language which makes no difference between she/he (Yeh, we're so cultured &amp; liberal!) &amp; this is why I frequently makes this mistake. I will try to avoid it in the future...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T06:22:31-07:00","id":858943,"title":"","content":"I think you've read that wrong. It was an early change. She changed after the first year rather than during a second year, <br /> Already been to Erebus, for reasons of the weaver rather than the wyrm. (actually, I got 4-point cursed In a fight with a glasswalker-theurge-turned-weaver-monstrosity because the storyteller was feeling mean, so I had to work it off)<br /> <br /> Learning gifts- We make it hard. Each spirit wants a fair bit of chimage, and most have a quest to go with them. When I went for grandmother's touch, bear sent me to settle a territory dispute between a pack of wendigo and a Ghural. Don't think I've ever worked so hard for a gift) <br /> On the other hand, I've been really light on fetishes, and I suppose that's because my character doesn't want to rely on external tools, but I think it's an odd job that fetishes are free when gifts aren't. <br /> <br /> She's not black from both sides of the family. Probably Uktena blood that many get would consider unsavoury. Somewhere along the line there's probably an ajaba, since the uktena do rather like the fera kinfolk of the africans. But, She's not met her true parent, and the one ancestor she has got (a Get ahroun) has provided no answers for her. <br /> Possible answers<br /> Lupus Get mother, Ajaba kinfolk father<br /> Uktena on one side with african blood, Get on the other. <br /> Transformy magic.<br /> <br /> I just wanted to be that one black character at the Klan meeting, without the full dose of worthlessness you'd get playing a fianna metis. <br /> <br /> He's getting better. Slowly, but he is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T06:42:16-07:00","id":858957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854508-migrating-to-the-beast-courts?p=858934#post858934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Asmodai!<br /> <br /> Yeh, I know the difference (by the way, Odin &amp; Wotan are tha names of a semi-equivalent deity based on different region/religion). In WoD Odin &amp; Wotan are both mentioned as a hell of an old Gangrel &amp; they may be the same old bloodsucker.<br /> <br /> About Karin: Sorry, English is only my second language &amp; I mainly speak a language which makes no difference between she/he (Yeh, we're so cultured &amp; liberal!) &amp; this is why I frequently makes this mistake. I will try to avoid it in the future...</div> </div> </div> </div>She's literaly called Karin (a female germanic name) daughter (d\u00f6ttir) of the chieftain/leader (Jarl).<br /> She's the character depicted on the cover of the Get of Fenris Revised tribebook (with a portrait in the back), and as the Get of Fenris and Philodox signature character in the revised Core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T09:24:46-07:00","id":859063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854508-migrating-to-the-beast-courts?p=858957#post858957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> She's literaly called Karin (a female germanic name) daughter (d\u00f6ttir) of the chieftain/leader (Jarl).<br /> She's the character depicted on the cover of the Get of Fenris Revised tribebook (with a portrait in the back), and as the Get of Fenris and Philodox signature character in the revised Core.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is perfectly clear. I just sometimes use &quot;he&quot; instead of &quot;she&quot; world. (Because it's shorter? Probably.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> About the ancestry:<br /> Leave it to two kinfolks. &quot;Love&quot; marriages with outsiders are not common in a Tribe which is so proud (&amp; agressively defensive) of their heritage as the Gets.<br /> <br /> And to totaly hijack this topic:<br /> <br /> You simultaneously play male / female characters? Some of my pals tried this, but that is awful when you try to seduce the full-extra sorceress who is played by an overweight, greasy haired boyscout.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T09:48:31-07:00","id":859077,"title":"","content":"I'm male, I play a female in this game, a male in another, a female in another, a male in two more. But I'm average in looks, In a stable relationship and... He's a little bit more difficult because he's the boyscout you described and plays exclusively attractive women as a workaround for his homosexuality and insecurity (that's the way he puts it), and we alternate between GM and Player. I don't put a female voice on when I'm playing a character, and I actively embrace the awkward; We've had sex scenes and all. I think he struggles a little with me because I'm a bit more creative and tend to have stuff I want to do and he sometimes doesn't like it when I circumvent something he'd set up with a plan, and sometimes I struggle with him because if he wants to do stuff, it's going to be to slow down and have character interaction; Multiple choices on how he tackles a situation don't tend to go well. But I enjoy the games, even if he does get anxiety about his performance as a storyteller/player. <br /> <br /> Two kinfolk making you black doesn't work when you're a lupus with the teltale get build (also, two dots of pure breed) <br /> Also, On paper, the Get of fenrir aren't supposed to give a shit about ancestors, race, gender, ethnicity, who your parents were or where you're from; So long as you're strong. I really like that Ideology and think it's a great driving force for a player character. It just doesn't work as well as it should because most get do have their issues, but that's not how Fenrir intended it. <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, Wave sentai<br /> - Do they have rolls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T10:06:54-07:00","id":859087,"title":"","content":"Kinfolks can have Pure Breed, which you could inherit. You could be the product of a wolf-repopulation program.<br /> <br /> I disagree, they can be very conservative. Even the females can have difficult times, because they are traditionaly male-controlled. And the Get was one of a great driving force in the 3rd Reich's, with the \u00fcbermensch attitude.<br /> <br /> The Wave Sentai: No they havent. They are just a bunch of Shens who works toward a single goal, except:<br /> Throw in a Nezumi or Kitsune (they usually borrow Rites) who have the Rite of Dedication (Ratkin Tribebook) &amp; it will be able to form a temporary Pack with a totem choosen to be the most effective in the said mission.<br /> After them the Pack specified Rites &amp; Gifts would work &amp; the Pack Tactics are avaiable.<br /> <br /> So 2 of you play with the ST/Player status constantly changing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T19:18:56-07:00","id":859391,"title":"","content":"I don't see why your character would want to JOIN the Beast Courts. However, I can completely understand why she might want to visit them/learn from them/ally herself to them. Why would she have to join?<br /> Leaving the Garou Nation and joining the Beast Courts isn't like changing your favorite sports team. It requires a lot of fundamental changes to that person's philosophy, spirituality, alliances and connection to the Spirits. Joining the Beast Courts means adopting a significantly different cosmology and view of the Wyrm and the Apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7861-strafe","name":"Strafe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}